4	 * Dependency-free, in-memory sliding-window rate limiter.
5	 *
6	 * Suitable for single-process app-level throttling (login attempts, etc).
7	 * State lives in a module-level Map; on a horizontally-scaled deployment each
8	 * instance limits independently — acceptable for auth-abuse mitigation. A
9	 * background sweep prunes empty buckets so the Map does not grow unbounded.
10	 */
